 ill River\, guaranteeing the city and the river a prominent place in Ameri
 can history. Over time\, the Schuylkill has served the city and its indust
 ry\, first with a canal system and later with railroads and highways in th
 e river’s flood plain. Factories and mills were built along its full len
 gth. Industry radically changed the river. Along with bringing farm produc
 ts and coal to the city. The Schuylkill River provided drinking water.…\
